On 7/11/06, Yanis Batura <ybatura@mail.ru> wrote:
> > sentence: {ko catlu le nu le smacu ku bajra}
>
> Can one look at an event?

Sure.

> If yes, can one look at other NU abstractions?

{za'i}, {pu'u}, {zu'o} and {co'i} yes, they are all kinds of {nu}.
These are things that take place in space-time, so there is
nothing strange about looking at them.

{du'u} and {ka}, no. These are not spatio-temporal objects.
{jei} is a kind of {du'u} and {ni} is a kind of {ka} (at least sometimes).

{li'i}, {su'u}... I don't really know what they mean.

The CLL example for {su'u} is:

   ko zgana le su'u le ci smacu cu bajra

mu'o mi'e xorxes


